  "summary": "I am a Full Stack Engineer with strong expertise in building secure, scalable, and cloud-native enterprise applications. My experience spans backend, frontend, and cloud platforms, enabling me to design end-to-end solutions that deliver both performance and security at scale.\n\nAt Citrix, I have contributed to Zero Trust Network Access (ZTNA) initiatives, architected microservices in Golang, Python, and Java, and developed micro-frontends in ReactJS to empower enterprise IT with secure access and device management capabilities. I’ve also designed and implemented integrations with industry-leading platforms such as Microsoft Intune, Okta, and CrowdStrike, leveraging OAuth 2.0 and Graph APIs to strengthen identity and device security.\n\nMy technical background includes hands-on work with Java, Golang, Python, ReactJS, NodeJS, Spring, Flask, Docker, Kubernetes, Terraform, and Jenkins, along with deep experience in monitoring and observability using Prometheus, Grafana, Splunk, and New Relic. I have delivered solutions that use MongoDB, CosmosDB, Redis, MySQL, and MSSQL to support enterprise-scale applications with high reliability.\n\nI enjoy working across the stack—whether it’s designing microservices architectures, optimizing backend APIs, or building modern frontend experiences—while always keeping scalability, reliability, and security in focus. With a Master’s in Computer Science from the University of Florida (CGPA 3.83/4.0), I bring both technical depth and problem-solving skills to every project.\n\nI am excited about opportunities to apply my expertise in full stack engineering, cloud applications, and security-driven solutions to create lasting business impact.",
